.TH SENSOR-BME680 1 "September 2026" "sensor-bme680 2.3.0" "WildlifeSystems"
.SH NAME
sensor-bme680 \- read BME680 environmental sensors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sensor-bme680
[\fB\-\-version\fR|\fB\-v\fR|\fBversion\fR|\fBidentify\fR|\fBlist\fR|\fBsetup\fR|\fBenable\fR|\fBmock\fR|\fBtemperature\fR|\fBhumidity\fR|\fBpressure\fR|\fBgas\fR|\fBinternal\fR|\fBexternal\fR|\fBall\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sensor-bme680
reads temperature, humidity, pressure and gas resistance from Bosch BME680
environmental sensors connected via I2C, and outputs the readings as a JSON
array in the WildlifeSystems format, one reading per measurement. It is
normally run by
.BR sr (1).
.SH COMMANDS
Not specifying a command is equivalent to \fBall\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-version, \-v, version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B identify
Exit with code 60, identifying the program as a WildlifeSystems sensor driver.
.TP
.B list
List the measurements provided, one per line: temperature, humidity, pressure
and gas. Each is also accepted as a command.
.TP
.B temperature, humidity, pressure, gas
Output only that measurement from every sensor.
.TP
.B setup
Report that no setup is required. The command is provided so that every driver
answers the same commands.
.TP
.B enable
Enable the I2C interface by adding \fIdtparam=i2c_arm=on\fR to the Raspberry Pi
boot configuration, or report that it is already enabled. Requires root. A
reboot is required after the directive is first added.
.TP
.B mock
Output fixed readings in the real output format, for testing without hardware:
23.5\[de]C, 45% humidity, 1013.25 hPa and 50000 Ohms, at location
\fI{{node}}\fR.
.TP
.B internal
Output only readings from sensors configured as internal.
.TP
.B external
Output only readings from sensors configured as external.
.TP
.B all
Output every measurement from every sensor.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file
.I /etc/ws/sensors/bme680.json
is a JSON array with one object per sensor. Without the file, a single sensor
is detected automatically at address 0x76 or 0x77. Each object may contain the
following fields.
.TP
.B i2c_addr
The I2C address as a string, "0x76" or "0x77". If omitted, the address is
detected automatically.
.TP
.B internal
Whether the sensor is inside the enclosure. The default is false.
.TP
.B sensor_id
A custom sensor identifier. If omitted, the identifier is
\fI<serial>_bme680\fR, where \fI<serial>\fR is the Raspberry Pi serial number.
Where more than one entry omits it, each is instead \fI<serial>_bme680_0x76\fR
or \fI<serial>_bme680_0x77\fR, so that two sensors do not share an identifier.
Each measurement appends its own name, giving for example
\fI<serial>_bme680_temperature\fR.
.TP
.B sensor_name
A human-readable name, reported in the \fBsensor_name\fR field.
.TP
.B location
Where the sensor is: the string \fI{{node}}\fR for the position of the node,
\fI{{none}}\fR for a sensor that has no position, or an object with
\fBlatitude\fR and \fBlongitude\fR in decimal degrees and, optionally,
\fBaltitude\fR and \fBaccuracy\fR in metres. If omitted, the \fBlocation\fR
field of the reading is null.
.PP
An example configuration:
.PP
.nf
[
  {
    "i2c_addr": "0x76",
    "internal": false,
    "sensor_name": "Weather station",
    "location": "{{node}}"
  }
]
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
A JSON array with one reading per measurement of each sensor. Each reading has
the fields of the
.BR sc-prototype (1)
template. The fields filled in by this driver are as follows.
.TP
.B sensor
"bme680_temperature", "bme680_humidity", "bme680_pressure" or
"bme680_gas_resistance".
.TP
.B device
"bme680".
.TP
.B measures
"temperature", "humidity", "pressure" or "resistance".
.TP
.B unit
"Celsius", "percentage", "hPa" or "Ohms".
.TP
.B value
The reading, to three decimal places, or null if the reading failed.
.TP
.B error
The reason the reading failed, or null. A reading never has both a value and
an error.
.TP
.B sensor_id, sensor_name, internal, location
Taken from the configuration, as described above.
.TP
.B timestamp
The Unix time at which the sensor was read.
.TP
.B config
The software version, the I2C address at which the sensor was read, and the
calibration parameters used for the measurement.
.PP
The \fBnode_id\fR and \fBdeployment_id\fR fields are left null and are filled
in by
.BR sr (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ws/sensors/bme680.json
The configuration file.
.TP
.I /dev/i2c-1
The I2C bus from which the sensors are read.
.TP
.I /boot/firmware/config.txt
The Raspberry Pi boot configuration, edited by \fBenable\fR
(\fI/boot/config.txt\fR on older systems).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 20
An invalid argument, or the readings could not be produced at all, for example
because \fBsc-prototype\fR was unavailable. Nothing is printed in that case.
.TP
.B 60
The \fBidentify\fR command.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sr (1),
.BR sc-prototype (1),
.BR i2cdetect (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Ed Baker <ed@ebaker.me.uk>
